description:
Read the headers of a 64-bit PE file from its bytes (lesson 1.03), and convert RVAs to file offsets:

```cpp
struct Section
{
    std::string name;
    std::uint32_t virtualAddress, virtualSize, rawPointer, rawSize, characteristics;
};

struct Headers
{
    std::uint16_t machine;
    std::uint32_t entryPoint;
    std::uint64_t imageBase;
    std::vector<Section> sections;
};

std::optional<Headers> readHeaders(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& file);
std::optional<std::uint32_t> rvaToOffset(const Headers& h, std::uint32_t rva);
```

**readHeaders** returns `std::nullopt` unless the file starts with `MZ`, has the `PE\0\0` signature at `e_lfanew` (offset 0x3C), and an optional header magic of `0x20B`, with every header inside the file. The section table starts right after the optional header, whose size is in the file header. Section names are up to 8 characters, without the zero padding.

**rvaToOffset** finds the section with `virtualAddress <= rva < virtualAddress + virtualSize` and returns `rva - virtualAddress + rawPointer`, or `std::nullopt` if no section contains it or the RVA is past the section's `rawSize` (in its zero-filled tail).

